@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+# Grounded time together
+
+Add a player-chosen Dance together moment and a Dance wardrobe preview. It is a finite 2800ms response, using the existing resident/preview clock, with two slow side-to-side sways. Both feet retain their ground contacts. There is no hop, reward accent, added sound, autonomous trigger, queue, or new timer.
+
+The torso moves at most 2.5 SVG units before species/mood scaling, leans at most 4.5 degrees, and gently shifts weight with at most 1.2% compression. Hands stay lightly raised and sweep with the rhythm; Mochi remains softer, Bun livelier, and Sprout smaller. Appendages lag with bounded low amplitude and ease to rest. Smooth envelopes give neutral geometry and zero speed at finite endpoints. The existing pleased-face blend and lifetime blink are retained.
+
+Integrate through PlayerGesture and existing reaction priority/deadline handling. Explicit repeated choices stay busy and never extend or queue the response; chore celebrations can interrupt. Sick/away residents retain their resting/check-in behavior. Reduced motion presents the existing still pleased expression until the semantic deadline, with no continuous idle clock. Successful speech remains owned by the resident, and no saved data changes.
+
+Six choices form balanced rows that adapt to container width and enlarged root text. The wardrobe uses the existing Stop, Pause/Resume, Mirror, pose cancellation, visibility and preference handling. Preview movement never redraws the item grid or changes saved wardrobe data.
+
+Verify finite endpoints, bounded speed/amplitude, feet, scaling, reduced motion, action priority, fractional walking interruption and tap alternation first. Then verify preview lifecycle and native keyboard/player speech/actual screen-space foot contacts. Review sampled character sheets for all species, both facings, default/dark colors and representative layered outfits at room and preview scales. Inspect responsive controls at narrow, landscape and desktop sizes with 100% and 200% root text. Still frames establish visible geometry; they do not certify temporal comfort or physical devices.
+
+This scope is authorized by the user's continuing request to improve character visuals, animations and features. It begins after the frozen outfit review and small heart-glasses correction have recoverable checkpoints. Heavy work remains sequential and resource-gated.
